    <div class="col-md-9">
        <h1>Documentation</h1>

        <section id="getting-started" class="mb-5">
            <h2>Getting started (for platform users)</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Register">Create an account</a> &mdash; anyone can sign up and use the platform for their own websites and apps.</li>
                <li>Go to <a asp-controller="Applications" asp-action="Index">My Applications</a> and register a new application for each website or app you want to collect feedback from.</li>
                <li>Open the application and click <strong>Generate new key</strong>. Copy the key immediately &mdash; it is shown only once. You'll also get a ready-to-run <code>curl</code> command.</li>
                <li>Optionally add <strong>custom fields</strong> to the application (e.g. "browser", "device_type") that your feedback form should collect.</li>
                <li>Start sending feedback from your app using the API below. It shows up on your <a asp-controller="Dashboard" asp-action="Index">Dashboard</a> and <a asp-controller="Feedback" asp-action="Index">Feedback</a> pages, and (if configured) you'll get an email each time.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>Platform administrators can see feedback and applications from every user, and configure API rate limits.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="api-auth" class="mb-5">
            <h2>API authentication</h2>
            <p>Every request to the feedback API must include the API key for the application it belongs to, in the <code>X-Api-Key</code> header:</p>
            <pre class="p-2 bg-dark text-light rounded"><code>X-Api-Key: fbk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</code></pre>
            <p>Keys are generated from the <a asp-controller="Applications" asp-action="Index">application page</a> and can be revoked at any time. A revoked key is rejected immediately.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="submit-feedback" class="mb-5">
            <h2>Submit feedback</h2>
            <p><code>POST /api/v1/feedback</code></p>
            <p>Required fields: <code>appVersion</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>comment</code>, <code>starRating</code> (1&ndash;5). Optional: <code>reporterName</code>, <code>reporterContact</code>, <code>customFields</code>. The server automatically records the caller's IP address.</p>

            <pre class="p-2 bg-dark text-light rounded"><code>curl -X POST https://your-domain.example/api/v1/feedback \
  -H "X-Api-Key: fbk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
        "appVersion": "1.4.2",
        "title": "Great app!",
        "comment": "Loving it so far, though the export button is hard to find.",
        "starRating": 5,
        "reporterName": "Jane Doe",
        "reporterContact": "jane@example.com",
        "customFields": {
          "browser_name": "Chrome"
        }
      }'</code></pre>

            <p>A successful call returns <code>201 Created</code> with the new feedback's id.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="custom-fields" class="mb-5">
            <h2>Custom fields</h2>
            <p>
                Each application can define its own extra fields (text, number, boolean, date, or a fixed set of
                options) from the <a asp-controller="Applications" asp-action="Index">application page</a>. Required
                fields must be present in <code>customFields</code> or the submission is rejected with a
                <code>400</code> response naming the missing field.
            </p>
            <p>Client apps can fetch an application's current field schema at any time:</p>
            <pre class="p-2 bg-dark text-light rounded"><code>curl https://your-domain.example/api/v1/feedback/fields \
  -H "X-Api-Key: fbk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="rate-limiting" class="mb-5">
            <h2>Rate limiting</h2>
            <p>
                Each API key is limited to a number of requests per minute. There is a platform-wide default,
                and administrators may override the limit for any individual application. Exceeding the limit
                returns:
            </p>
            <pre class="p-2 bg-dark text-light rounded"><code>HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 60

{ "error": "Rate limit exceeded.", "limitPerMinute": 60 }</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="errors" class="mb-5">
            <h2>Errors</h2>
            <p>Errors are returned as an RFC 7807 <code>application/problem+json</code> body:</p>
            <table class="table table-sm">
                <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>400</td><td>Validation failed (missing/invalid field, or a required custom field)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>401</td><td>Missing, invalid, or revoked API key</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>404</td><td>Referenced resource not found</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>429</td><td>Rate limit exceeded</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>500</td><td>Unexpected server error</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
